{
  "summary": "This experiment tested a multimodal model combining scvi_n200 (RNA) and ViT (image) encoders with concat fusion in singleprofile settings, achieving validation accuracy of 0.532 (F1: 0.517). The result is lower than the best RNA-only baseline (scvi_n200 in multiprofile, 0.650) but higher than image-only baselines (0.207), suggesting multimodal approaches may offer limited benefit in this configuration. The exact impact of fusion strategy or image encoder strength remains uncertain without direct comparison to alternative modalities or aggregation methods."
}

